content.text:
verdict: findings
draft_version_seen: 2
checks:
  - {claim: "Summary 1 / F1 — Cagan", question: "Do 'very weak product', 'no clear owner', 'one person', and 'is really a backlog administrator' appear in Cagan's pages, and is the last one about the PM under the CSPO conception?", source_reopened: "https://www.svpg.com/product-manager-vs-product-owner/ ; .../product-manager-vs-product-owner-revisited/ ; .../behind-every-great-product/", result: pass, notes: "All four verbatim; 'In this model, the product manager is really a backlog administrator' is tied to the CSPO-based conception as the draft states."}
  - {claim: "Summary 1 / F1 — Scrum Guide", question: "Do the delegation, 'one person, not a committee', and 'respect their decisions' quotes exist verbatim?", source_reopened: "https://scrumguides.org/scrum-guide.html", result: pass, notes: "All verbatim."}
  - {claim: "Summary 1 / F1 — SAFe PM/PO", question: "Do the PM/PO definition quotes appear on the public abstracts, and is 'only team member empowered to accept stories as done' correctly marked secondhand?", source_reopened: "https://framework.scaledagile.com/product-management/ ; https://framework.scaledagile.com/product-owner/ (abstracts, login-walled)", result: pass, notes: "Abstract quotes verbatim; the acceptance line is absent from the public page and does appear on third-party pages (Global Knowledge, O'Reilly SAFe 4.0 guide) — evidence E2 should name those instead of 'search snippet'."}
  - {claim: "Summary 1 / F1 — Pragmatic", question: "Do 'messenger of the market', 'development-facing role... key stakeholder', 'run faster'/'right direction' exist verbatim?", source_reopened: "https://www.pragmaticinstitute.com/resources/articles/product/comprehensive-guide-product-owner-vs-product-manager/", result: pass, notes: "All verbatim."}
  - {claim: "Summary 2 / F2", question: "Do Cagan's four-risks and start-here lines, Perri's secondhand lines, Pragmatic's 'tell the development organization about the problem', and MtP's 'no positional power' exist as quoted?", source_reopened: "https://www.svpg.com/four-big-risks/ ; https://www.svpg.com/product-management-start-here/ ; https://www.produxlabs.com/product-thinking-blog/episode-252-project-product-management ; https://www.mindtheproduct.com/escaping-build-trap-melissa-perri/ ; https://www.pragmaticinstitute.com/resources/articles/product/role-of-product-management/ ; https://www.mindtheproduct.com/product-management-growth-team-effort/", result: pass, notes: "All verbatim; the 'Agile does not have a brain... never has, told you what to build' elision spans two adjacent sentences and is shown with an ellipsis."}
  - {claim: "Summary 3 / F3 — Scrum Guide", question: "Are the four backlog bullets, sizing line, and DoD line accurate, with the DoD paraphrase marked?", source_reopened: "https://scrumguides.org/scrum-guide.html", result: pass, notes: "Verbatim; the DoD line labelled 'paraphrasing' is in fact an exact quote — harmless but could be un-marked."}
  - {claim: "Summary 3 / F3 — Cucumber", question: "Do 'Three Amigos... three voices', 'scope of the application', 'generating lots of Scenarios', 'add many of the Steps', 'actively reviewed by the product owner', 'identify the problem', 'acceptance criteria the team has agreed upon', 'learned the most', and 'weak-ass move' exist verbatim?", source_reopened: "https://cucumber.io/docs/bdd/who-does-what/ ; https://cucumber.io/docs/bdd/discovery-workshop/ ; https://cucumber.io/blog/bdd/who-writes-the-cucumber-scenarios/", result: pass, notes: "All verbatim; source has 'constraints/acceptance criteria' — the draft's fragment is faithful."}
  - {claim: "F3 — Humanizing Work", question: "Do 'mix of business and technical perspectives' and 'concrete change in system behavior' exist verbatim?", source_reopened: "https://www.humanizingwork.com/the-humanizing-work-guide-to-splitting-user-stories/", result: pass, notes: "Both verbatim on second targeted read."}
  - {claim: "Summary 4 / F4 — Cohn", question: "Do 'what to build, not how to build it' and 'sparingly, wisely and ideally, in consultation with the team' exist verbatim?", source_reopened: "https://www.mountaingoatsoftware.com/blog/can-a-product-owner-dictate-the-architecture", result: pass, notes: "Verbatim."}
  - {claim: "Summary 4 / F4 — Wolpers", question: "Do the 'How'/'What' anti-pattern sentence, 'built-in checks & balances', 'only person to decide', 'ticket monkey', 'waterfall 2.0' exist verbatim?", source_reopened: "https://age-of-product.com/product-owner-anti-patterns/", result: pass, notes: "All verbatim, including the parenthetical."}
  - {claim: "Summary 4 / F4 — Xebia", question: "Do 'ultimately made by the product owner', 'explaining and promoting', 'valid business case' exist verbatim?", source_reopened: "https://xebia.com/blog/architects-scrum-4-what-is-the-role-of-the-architect-in-scrum/", result: pass, notes: "Verbatim."}
  - {claim: "F4 — SAFe System Architect / NFR abstracts", question: "Do 'defining enablers... managing capacity for enablement work' and 'revisited as part of the definition of done' appear on the public abstracts?", source_reopened: "https://framework.scaledagile.com/system-architect/ ; https://framework.scaledagile.com/nonfunctional-requirements/", result: pass, notes: "Both verbatim on the visible abstract; body login-walled as declared."}
  - {claim: "F4 — agileseekers practitioner quote", question: "Does the sentence 'Product Owners and Managers should work closely with architects to ensure that these items are appropriately tracked and prioritized appropriately in the backlog' exist verbatim?", source_reopened: "https://agileseekers.com/blog/collaborating-with-system-architects-to-refine-non-functional-enablers", result: fail, notes: "Source reads 'By collaborating with architects, PO/PMs can ensure that these items are appropriately tracked and prioritized in the backlog.' — draft's quotation is a rewrite (and doubles 'appropriately'); it also disagrees with evidence E15's own wording. Replace with the verbatim sentence or mark as paraphrase."}
  - {claim: "Summary 5 / F5 — Torres", question: "Do 'typically comprised of', 'at a minimum', 'jointly responsible for a shared outcome', the three 'together' sentences, and the 'mercenary teams' line exist as quoted?", source_reopened: "https://www.producttalk.org/product-trio/", result: pass, notes: "All verbatim; the mercenary sentence is 'often results in designers and engineers working as what Marty Cagan ... calls \"mercenary teams\" instead of \"missionary teams\"' — the draft's ellipsis hides that Torres attributes the term to Cagan; acceptable but worth noting."}
  - {claim: "Summary 5 / F5 — Illustrated Agile, decode.agency, Aha!", question: "Do the architect-feasibility, 'ultimately responsible for product decisions', 'most important task', and 'work with system architects... allocate capacity' quotes exist verbatim?", source_reopened: "https://illustratedagile.com/2012/07/10/powerful-partnership-product-owner-designer-architects/ ; https://decode.agency/article/solution-architect-in-product-discovery/ ; https://www.aha.io/roadmapping/guide/product-development-methodologies/what-is-the-role-of-pm-in-safe", result: pass, notes: "All verbatim."}
  - {claim: "F5 — LogRocket sample RACI", question: "Is the PM Accountable at every stage and the architect Responsible only in Design, and does 'ONE single person' exist?", source_reopened: "https://blog.logrocket.com/product-management/sample-raci-chart-best-practices-template/", result: pass, notes: "Quote verbatim; architect is R in Design and Consulted at Discover/Deliver — 'Responsible in design only' holds, though 'consulted elsewhere' would be fuller."}
  - {claim: "Summary 6 / F6", question: "Do the feature-factory bullets, Perri's 'no measures of success', Larson's 'waiter... order taker' and 'passed down feature requests', Meegle's 'power struggles', and Spolsky's 'run out of oxygen' quotes exist as given?", source_reopened: "https://blog.logrocket.com/product-management/build-trap-dangers-feature-factory-mindset/ ; https://www.mindtheproduct.com/escaping-build-trap-melissa-perri/ ; https://lethain.com/notes-escaping-the-build-trap/ ; https://www.meegle.com/en_us/topics/raci-matrix/raci-matrix-for-product-ownership ; https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Architecture_astronaut", result: pass, notes: "All verbatim; the draft's summary compresses 'The waiter is a product manager who, at heart, is an order taker' into '\"a waiter\"' — fragment is faithful."}
  - {claim: "Summary 7 / F7", question: "Do Cagan's four risks assign usability to a designer and does Torres require a designer at minimum?", source_reopened: "https://www.svpg.com/four-big-risks/ ; https://www.producttalk.org/product-trio/", result: pass, notes: "'The Product Designer is responsible for the usability risk' and 'at a minimum' both verbatim; the gap is labelled as the report's observation."}
confidence_labels: "all defensible — item 1 and F1 split 'high on sources / medium on reconciliation' are two confidence labels, not confidence mixed with likelihood; F4 medium fits practitioner-plus-abstract sourcing; F2/F3/F5 high each rest on at least two fully opened primaries."
top_changes: ["F4: replace the agileseekers quotation with the verbatim sentence 'By collaborating with architects, PO/PMs can ensure that these items are appropriately tracked and prioritized in the backlog.' (or mark as paraphrase) and align evidence E15 to the same wording", "F1 / evidence E2: name the actual secondhand carriers of 'the only team member empowered to accept stories as done' (e.g. Global Knowledge SAFe POPM page; O'Reilly SAFe 4.0 Reference Guide ch.18) instead of 'search snippet' so the draft's 'third-party training and reference pages' is traceable", "F5: optionally show that Torres attributes 'mercenary teams / missionary teams' to Cagan, since the ellipsis currently drops the attribution", "F3: drop the 'paraphrasing' marker on the Definition-of-Done line — it is an exact quote"]
